SECTION II. 
Main design features 
 
Most of standard dipole design features remain the same. The yoke geometry is straight (not curved) in the longitudinal direction, it has an H cross-section and is trapezoidal when viewed from the top. The NbTi coils also have a trapezoidal shape and keep the standard cross-section (560 turns of 2.23 × 1.43 mm conductor). Requirements for the Super-FRS standard dipoles shown in Table I must also be met by Super-FRS branched dipoles. The magnetic design of the standard Super-FRS dipoles has been modified to allow the installation of the Y-shaped vacuum chamber shown on Fig. 2 . Consequently, the standard coil casing must be split into two independent casings leading to a major modification of the cryostat design (mechanical, cryogenics). This doubles the number of cold-to-warm supports and they require larger opening on the side of the yoke reducing even more the initial volume of iron. Therefore approximately 1.8% of the standard dipole yoke volume must be removed which increases the total amp-turns needed to reach the field integral requirement. 
