SECTION III. 
Preliminary magnetic analyses 
A. Magnetic simulations 
 
The magnetic design has been analyzed with Opera 3D [6] using the same electrical steel B-H curve as the one of the prototype tested in 2011 by the Institute of Modern Physics (IMP) [7] , [8] . Table II allows to compare the magnetic simulation results obtained for standard (Std) and branched (Br.) dipoles. Note that both dipole types will provide a bending angle of 9.75 ∘ . The following parameters are gathered in Table II for comparison purpose: the peak field on conductor ( B p e a k ), the current (I) to reach the flux density at the magnet center ( B 0 ) and the stored energy (E). All these parameters show that more current (or amp.turns) is needed for the branched magnet version to reach the same field at the center ( B 0 ). As a consequence, this increases the peak field on the conductor and the stored energy but they remain manageable from the quench protection point of view. 
