Fig. 3 shows the integrated field homogeneity of the branched dipole. Note that the homogeneity shown on Fig. 3 has been obtained through the optimization of the end chamfers geometry. For example, the alignment slot and the holes for the screws have been slightly moved to the sides to improve the homogeneity. These chamfer holes asymmetries can actually be seen on Fig. 5 . Looking at the homogeneity map, one can locate the chamfers holes through the blue to red areas at z = ± 70 mm. Morever there are two spots in the midplane located at y = ± 190 mm which shows the homogeneity perturbation which were almost compensated by the chamfers. These homogeneity perturbations are due to the openings in the yoke that are required for the installation of the four horizontal cold-to-warm-supports (CTWS) and the Y-shaped vacuum chamber. 
