SECTION VI. 
Summary 
 
A preliminary design gathering all the concept principles have been presented in this paper for the FAIR Super-FRS superferric branched dipoles. The insertion of the Y-shaped vacuum chamber makes the flux density distribution more asymmetric than it already is on the standard dipoles due to the trapezoidal shape of the coils and yoke. The design is rather well defined from the electromagnetic point of view but there are still few analyses to carry out on the mechanical and cryogenics aspect. Mechanical analyses will be led to evaluate the split coil casing concept requiring cold-to-warm contacts which draw increased heat load to the coil casing. The active thermosiphon concept proposed is promising and transient analyses will be finalized to take into account CTWCs. CEA plans on proposing a final design to FAIR/GSI during the Summer of 2018. 
 
